.\" Install: doas install -m 644 docs/man/cdda2img.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
.TH CDDA2IMG 1 "2026\-07\-30" "cdda2img 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.\"
.SH NAME
cdda2img \- create and extract RBI audio CD archive images
.\"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "cdda2img rip"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B "cdda2img create"
.RI [ options ]
.I INPUT_DIR
.br
.B "cdda2img extract"
.RI [ options ]
.I FILE.rbi
.br
.B "cdda2img import"
.RI [ options ]
.I SOURCE
.br
.B "cdda2img burn"
.RI [ options ]
.I FILE.rbi
.br
.B "cdda2img list"
.RI [ options ]
.I FILE.rbi
.br
.B "cdda2img test"
.I FILE.rbi
.br
.B "cdda2img catalogue"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B "cdda2img mount"
.RI [ options ]
.I FILE.rbi
.br
.B "cdda2img setup"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B "cdda2img doctor"
.br
.B "cdda2img \-\-version"
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cdda2img
archives CD\-DA (Red Book audio) discs and collections of audio files
as RBI (Red Book Image) container images.
An RBI file stores the disc\(cqs raw PCM audio (signed 16\-bit little\-endian,
44100\~Hz stereo), an embedded cdrdao\-format TOC, optional blocks for EBU\~R128
ReplayGain data, AccurateRip verification results, rip provenance, and rip log,
and per\-block BLAKE3 integrity checksums in a single self\-contained file.
The current format version is RBI v6.0.
.PP
Metadata \(em album title, artist, per\-track titles, ISRC codes, and original\-release
provenance \(em is sourced interactively from MusicBrainz, AcoustID, and Discogs
lookups and embedded in the TOC block.
.\"
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS rip \(em Rip
Rips a physical CD\-DA disc to an RBI image.
Rip captures audio verbatim: raw PCM is encapsulated in the RBI container
1:1, with no silence trimming or gap insertion (this is intrinsic to the
ripping path \(em there is no
.B \-\-silence
flag on
.BR rip ).
.PP
The rip is a single pass on a single spin\-up, through
.BR AccuDisc .
One read captures raw s16le audio, the C2 error bitmap, the raw P\-W subchannel,
and the lead\-in\(cqs full TOC and CD\-Text.
Track boundaries are taken from the error\-corrected full TOC; pre\-gaps, INDEX
points, CONTROL flags, the MCN (Q\-channel Mode 2) and per\-track ISRCs
(Q\-channel Mode 3) are assembled from the Q stream by majority vote across all
observations of each value.
There is no second metadata pass and no second engine: if the assembly fails, the
rip fails.
.PP
Majority voting is not a refinement.
It makes the ISRC read structurally immune to a class of defect \(em a decoder
that latches the first value it sees reports the
.I previous
track\(cqs code whenever an ISRC lies in a track\(cqs first sectors, which
silently prevents automatic release identification and is invisible in the
output.
A value that must win a vote across the whole track cannot be set by one frame.
.PP
If AccurateRip then reports a
.I partial
mismatch, two recovery exits are tried in cost order.
First
.IR "CTDB parity repair" :
Reed\-Solomon repair against crowd\-sourced parity from the CUETools database,
with zero extra reads, using the C2 bitmap as erasures where one was captured.
A repair is committed only if a CTDB per\-track CRC
.I and
AccurateRip both accept it.
Only if that declines does the drive spin again: each failed track\(cqs sector
window is re\-read across the drive\(cqs admitted speed ladder, fastest to
slowest, and the first AccurateRip\-verified result is spliced in
sample\-exactly.
A track that never matches keeps its original audio \(em an unverified splice is
never written.
.PP
Before each rip,
.B cdda2img rip
automatically resolves the correct drive sample offset.
Resolution order: (1) per-drive entry in the
.B [[drives]]
section of
.IR cdda2img.toml ;
(2) the AccurateRip drive offset catalog, auto-applied when the entry has
\(>=\~3 submissions and prompts interactively when confidence is lower;
(3) a read offset of 0 with a warning when the drive is not configured
and no AccurateRip match is applied.
A confirmed offset is saved to
.B [[drives]]
automatically so subsequent rips skip the catalog lookup.
.PP
After a successful rip, the per\-track AccurateRip v1/v2 checksums are computed
and verified against the AccurateRip database.
Results are printed as an informational report; a mismatch does not fail the rip.
.PP
.BI "cdda2img rip " "[options]"
.TP
.BI \-\-device " DEVICE"
Optical drive device node (default:
.BR /dev/sr0 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-loudness " {rg|none}"
Same semantics as for the
.B create
subcommand.
Default:
.BR rg .
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Output
.B .rbi
file path, or a directory in which to place an album\-derived filename.
If
.I PATH
is an existing directory the filename is derived from the album title and
written into that directory; otherwise
.I PATH
is treated as the explicit output file.
Default: the album\-derived filename in the current working directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-preview ", " \-\-no\-preview
Show a terminal album art preview and play track 1 in the background
during the rip.
Purely cosmetic; never blocks or fails the rip.
Default: from config
.RB ( preview ),
true.
.TP
.BR \-\-tui ", " \-\-no\-tui
Use the terminal UI for live rip progress.
.B \-\-no\-tui
renders progress to plain stdout without screen clearing.
No\-op when stdin is not a TTY.
Default: from config
.RB ( tui ),
true.
.TP
.BI \-\-duplicate " {skip|replace|add}"
How to handle an existing catalogue entry for this disc:
.B skip
aborts registration silently;
.B replace
deletes the existing entry and inserts the new one;
.B add
always inserts, allowing multiple entries per disc.
Overrides the
.B duplicate_catalogue_entry
configuration key for this run.
Default: from config, ask (prompt if TTY, skip otherwise).
.TP
.BR \-\-auto ", " \-\-no\-auto
Skip the interactive metadata menu and accept the best\-guess result
automatically.
See
.B METADATA MATCHING
for score details.
Overrides the
.B auto
configuration key for this run.
Default: from config, false.
.TP
.B \-\-extract
After the RBI container is written, immediately extract it to per\-track
FLAC files and a CUE sheet in an
.B extracted/
subdirectory of the current working directory.
The RBI file is kept unless
.B \-\-no\-keep\-rbi
is also supplied.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-keep\-rbi
Delete the RBI container after successful extraction.
Only meaningful with
.BR \-\-extract .
.\"
.SS create \(em Create
Creates one or more RBI images from a directory of audio files.
Files are grouped into CD\-sized batches (up to 99 tracks, up to 80 minutes)
according to the chosen batching strategy.
Each track is transcoded to Red Book PCM (44100\~Hz, 16\-bit, stereo) via PyAV.
.PP
.BI "cdda2img create " "[options] INPUT_DIR"
.TP
.BI \-\-silence " {trim|notrim}"
.RS
.TP
.B trim
Trims leading and trailing silence (threshold from
.B \-\-silence\-threshold ,
default \-55\~dBFS) and appends a 2\-second inter\-track gap per track.
This is the default.
.TP
.B notrim
Transcodes audio to Red Book PCM without further processing.
Silence trimming and inter\-track gap padding are disabled.
Use this mode for 1:1 preservation of source audio.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-silence\-threshold " N"
Silence detection threshold in \-dBFS (default: from config, 55).
Only applied when
.B \-\-silence trim
is in effect.
.TP
.BI \-\-loudness " {rg|none}"
.RS
.TP
.B rg
Measures EBU\~R128 integrated loudness and embeds a ReplayGain block containing
per\-track and album gain, peak, and LRA values.
This is the default.
.TP
.B none
Skips loudness analysis.
No ReplayGain block is written.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-strategy " {fcfs|aatc|best|meta}"
Disc batching strategy (default:
.BR aatc ).
.RS
.TP
.B fcfs
First\-come\-first\-served.
Fills a single disc in input file order; stops when full.
.TP
.B aatc
All\-as\-they\-come.
Fills discs in input file order, creating as many discs as needed.
.TP
.B best
Global bin\-packing to minimise the total number of discs; input order is
not preserved.
Requires OR\-Tools.
.TP
.B meta
Groups tracks by their embedded disc\-number tag; untagged tracks form a
final group.
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-preserve\-pregaps
Preserves pre\-gaps in trim mode (no\-op for audio\-file input).
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Output
.B .rbi
file path, or a directory to receive album\-derived filenames.
For multi\-disc batches the stem is used as a base name with a
.I _discN
suffix.
Default: album\-derived filename(s) in the current working directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-tui ", " \-\-no\-tui
Same as for the
.B rip
subcommand.
.TP
.BI \-\-duplicate " {skip|replace|add}"
Same as for the
.B rip
subcommand.
.TP
.BR \-\-auto ", " \-\-no\-auto
Same as for the
.B rip
subcommand.
.\"
.SS extract \(em Extract
Extracts one or more block types from an RBI image.
Output is written to an
.I extracted/
directory beneath the current working directory.
All flags are additive; omitting all flags is equivalent to
.BR \-\-all .
.PP
.BI "cdda2img extract " "[options] FILE.rbi"
.TP
.B \-\-tracks
Writes per\-track FLAC files with embedded metadata and a CUE sheet to
.IR extracted/<artist>/<album>/ .
ReplayGain Vorbis comment tags are embedded when an RG block is present,
unless
.B \-\-normalize
is also given.
If no RG block is present, loudness is measured from the extracted FLACs
and embedded post\-extraction.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Writes the embedded TOC
.RI ( .toc )
and PCM audio
.RI ( .wav ,
signed 16\-bit little\-endian in a self\-describing RIFF container) to
.IR extracted/ .
The TOC\(cqs
.B FILE
line references the
.B .wav
by name; in cdrdao\-TOC semantics a
.B .wav
file is read little\-endian, so filename and byte order agree.
.TP
.B \-\-rg
Writes the ReplayGain block as a JSON sidecar
.RI ( .rg.json ).
.TP
.B \-\-ar
Writes the AccurateRip verification report
.RI ( .accurip ).
.TP
.B \-\-log
Writes the rip log
.RI ( .log ).
.TP
.B \-\-all
Extracts all block types.
This is the default when no flags are given.
.TP
.B \-\-normalize
Applies EBU\~R128 normalisation to each extracted FLAC at \-18\~LUFS.
Active when
.B \-\-tracks
or
.B \-\-all
is set.
Mutually exclusive with ReplayGain tag embedding.
.\"
.SS import \(em Import
Imports a foreign disc image into an RBI container.
Import preserves the source audio verbatim: only byte\-order conversion
and container encapsulation are applied; there is no silence trim or
gap insertion (the source image already encodes the disc layout).
.PP
.BI "cdda2img import " "[options] SOURCE"
.PP
.I SOURCE
is one of:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
A cdrdao
.B .toc
file (the corresponding
.B .bin
must exist in the same directory).
.IP \(bu 4
A DDP\~2.0 image directory containing a
.B DDPID
file.
.IP \(bu 4
A Nero
.B .nrg
file (DAO CD-DA only; NER5 and NERO format variants; single-session).
.IP \(bu 4
A CloneCD
.B .ccd
file (the corresponding
.B .img
must exist in the same directory; audio tracks only; single-session).
.IP \(bu 4
A PlexTools
.B .pxi
file (single-session CD\-DA only).
The format is undocumented and was reverse\-engineered; embedded CD\-Text,
per\-track INDEX points and the MCN are recovered.
Where the stored audio stops short of a whole final sector the tail is
zero\-filled to the declared lead\-out and the amount is recorded in the
container's provenance as
.BR pxi_tail_padded .
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-loudness " {rg|none}"
Same semantics as for the
.B create
subcommand.
Default:
.BR rg .
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Output
.B .rbi
file path, or a directory in which to place an album\-derived filename.
If
.I PATH
is an existing directory the filename is derived from the album title and
written into that directory; otherwise
.I PATH
is treated as the explicit output file.
Default: the album\-derived filename in the current working directory.
.TP
.B \-\-info
Dry\-run mode: parse and display image metadata without importing.
No output file is written.
.TP
.BR \-\-tui ", " \-\-no\-tui
Same as for the
.B rip
subcommand.
.TP
.BI \-\-duplicate " {skip|replace|add}"
Same as for the
.B rip
subcommand.
.TP
.BR \-\-auto ", " \-\-no\-auto
Same as for the
.B rip
subcommand.
.\"
.SS burn \(em Burn
Burns an RBI image to a blank CD\-DA disc via AccuDisc
.RB ( "accudisc write \-\-toc \-\-bin" ),
feeding the stored raw s16le PCM directly (no byte\-swap).
Applies write offset correction to the disc stream before burning when a
.B write_offset
is configured for the drive in
.BR [[drives]] .
.PP
.BI "cdda2img burn " "[options] FILE.rbi"
.TP
.BI \-\-device " DEVICE"
CD drive device node (default:
.BR /dev/sr0 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " N"
Burn speed in CD\-DA drive units (default: 4).
.TP
.BI \-\-write\-offset " N"
Write offset override in samples.
Overrides the per\-drive
.B write_offset
from configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-simulate
Run the full write path with the laser off (test write), validating the
image and geometry without consuming a blank disc.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt before burning.
.\"
.SS list \(em List
Prints container information for an RBI image.
All flags are additive; omitting all flags is equivalent to
.BR \-\-info .
.PP
.BI "cdda2img list " "[options] FILE.rbi"
.TP
.B \-\-info
Prints the block directory with byte offsets, sizes, and checksums,
followed by a numbered track listing.
This is the default when no flags are given.
.TP
.B \-\-rg
Renders the ReplayGain block as text.
.TP
.B \-\-ar
Renders the AccurateRip verification report.
.TP
.B \-\-log
Renders the rip log.
.TP
.B \-\-prov
Dumps the raw provenance (PROV) block as decoded
.I key=value
lines, one per line, in file order.
Unlike
.BR \-\-info ,
which renders only a curated subset of provenance, this shows
.I every
key \(em including ones no other view surfaces, such as
.BR acoustid_gate ,
.BR release_tied_after ,
.BR release_selection ,
and
.BR multi_match_isrc_disambiguated .
When several MusicBrainz pressings matched the disc's TOC,
.B release_selection
records how the pinned one was chosen \(em
.BR unique ,
.BR auto_tiebreak ,
.BR manual ,
or
.BR rejected
\(em and only
.B auto_tiebreak
is a guess. Prefer
.B release_tied_after
over
.BR release_selected_via :
the latter names the first ranking key on which the candidates differ, which is
not necessarily the key that picked the winner.
Useful for auditing a library, e.g.
.IP
.EX
for f in *.rbi; do
  cdda2img list "$f" \-\-prov | grep \-q 'acoustid_gate=failed' \e
    && echo "$f"
done
.EE
.\"
.SS test \(em Test
Verifies the integrity and spec\-conformance of an RBI image.
Runs 27 checks covering magic bytes, format version, flags, block directory
structure, file size, UTF\-8 metadata, BLAKE3 checksums for all blocks
(SHA\-256 for legacy v4.x containers),
TOC parse, and track\-count consistency.
Exits with status 1 if any check fails.
.PP
.B "cdda2img test"
.I FILE.rbi
.\"
.SS catalogue \(em Browse catalogue
Displays an interactive disc catalogue browser.
The summary screen shows disc, track, and artist counts and lists the top artists;
press
.B s
to open the search screen or
.B q
to quit.
The search screen matches terms against artist name, album title, year, or track title.
From the paged results list, select a number to drill into the full per\-track detail
(including AccurateRip status and confidence), press
.B d
to delete an entry with confirmation, press
.B s
for a new search, or press
.B q
to quit.
Requires an interactive terminal.
.PP
.BI "cdda2img catalogue " "[options]"
.TP
.BI \-\-db " PATH"
Use the catalogue database at
.I PATH
instead of the default
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/cdda2img/cdda2img.db .
.\"
.SS mount \(em Mount
Mounts an RBI image as a virtual CD\-DA disc via cdemu.
The image is first extracted to a scratch directory (TOC + BIN),
then loaded into a free cdemu slot with
.BR "cdemu load" .
After mounting, the virtual disc is accessible to any application
that reads optical drives, including cdrdao for re-ripping.
.PP
.BI "cdda2img mount " "[options] FILE.rbi"
.TP
.BI \-\-slot " N"
cdemu device slot to load the image into (default: first free slot).
Fails if the specified slot is already loaded.
.TP
.BI \-\-mnt\-dir " PATH"
Directory for the extracted TOC and BIN scratch files
(default:
.IR ./mnt ).
.PP
After a successful mount,
.B cdda2img mount
prints the cdemu slot number, the TOC path, and reminder commands for
re-ripping and unloading.
The cdemu daemon must be running and the
.B vhba
kernel module must be loaded.
.\"
.SS setup \(em Setup wizard
Interactive setup wizard and maintenance tools.
When invoked without a subcommand flag, displays a menu of all available
sections. Each flag jumps directly to the named section without showing the menu.
.PP
.BI "cdda2img setup " "[options]"
.TP
.B \-\-create\-config
Copy the bundled template to
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml .
Prompts before overwriting an existing file.
.TP
.B \-\-update\-config
Overlay the current config onto the latest template, preserving all
user-set values. Makes a timestamped backup before writing.
.TP
.B \-\-validate\-config
Parse the config, report unknown keys, and offer to remove them.
.TP
.B \-\-read\-offset
Probe the drive name via sysfs, fetch the AccurateRip drive catalogue,
display the recommended read offset, and offer to save it to config.
.TP
.B \-\-write\-offset
Measure the drive write offset via burn-and-read-back cycles.
Each cycle burns a synthetic 75-second test signal to a blank disc,
rips it back, and locates the known noise pulses. Results accumulate in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/cdda2img/write_offset_<drive>.toml .
Prompts are paced with quotes from
.I 101 Uses For Your Write-Offset Test CDs
because every cycle consumes a blank disc.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " DEV"
CD drive device (default: from config
.IR default_device ).
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " N"
Burn speed for
.B \-\-write\-offset
cycles (default: 4).
.TP
.B \-\-create\-catalogue
Create the disc catalogue database if it does not exist.
.TP
.B \-\-validate\-catalogue
Run
.B PRAGMA integrity_check
and schema migration on the catalogue, and offer
.BR VACUUM .
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-catalogue
Check every catalogue entry: verify the RBI file exists and that its
blake3 checksum matches the stored value. Missing files trigger a
directory scan to locate a relocated copy. Mismatched checksums offer
to update or delete the record.
With
.BR \-\-test ,
also runs the full 27-rule structural verify (
.BR "cdda2img test" )
on every reachable entry.
.TP
.B \-\-test
When used with
.BR \-\-verify\-catalogue :
run the full container verify on each reachable entry (slow for large
catalogues).
.PP
The setup wizard fires automatically (as a warning + hint) when a required
file is missing at startup. It does not block the requested subcommand.
.\"
.SS doctor \(em Check dependencies
.B cdda2img doctor
reports every dependency \(em Python packages, the AccuDisc engine, the
external binaries, and the native libraries \(em with, for each missing one,
what it would have enabled and the command that would install it.
It takes no options.
.PP
It
.I checks
only. Nothing here installs, downloads, or modifies anything, and it makes
no network requests, so it is safe to run on a machine you are only
inspecting.
.PP
Exit status is
.B 1
if a
.I required
dependency is missing and
.B 0
otherwise.
A missing optional dependency is reported without failing: the absence of
.B ffplay
costs the rip\(cqs track\-1 preview, not the rip.
.PP
A shorter form of the same check runs automatically before every other
subcommand and refuses to start when a required Python package is missing,
listing all of them at once.
.PP
Three states are reported rather than two.
Besides
.B ok
and
.BR MISS ,
a
.B WARN
marks something that works on this machine and would not work on another \(em
notably an AccuDisc binding reachable only through the development shim in
.IR tools/accudisc/pybinding ,
which is present in a source checkout and nowhere else.
That state is deliberately not rendered as
.BR ok :
a report that certified an unreproducible machine as clean would be worse
than no report.
.\"
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the cdda2img version and exit.
.\"
.SH METADATA MATCHING
After every rip, import, and create pipeline completes the remote metadata
lookups (CDDB, MusicBrainz, AcoustID, Discogs), cdda2img computes a
.I match confidence score
that summarises how many independent signals agreed on the disc's identity.
The score is additive and is written as
.B match_confidence
in the RBI provenance block.
.PP
The score shown on screen is computed
.I before
the metadata menu opens, and describes how confident the automatic guess is.
The value written to the provenance block is computed
.I after
the menu closes, and describes what the container ended up believing. These
are deliberately two different numbers. If you confirm a pressing by hand, the
stored
.B match_confidence
is
.BR 1.000 ,
because a manual selection is not a guess; the score components below then do
not apply.
.SS Score components
Each signal contributes a fixed weight when present:
.TP
.B mb_disc_id  +0.50
A MusicBrainz disc ID SHA\-1 fingerprint uniquely identified a release.
This is the strongest signal: it is derived from the exact physical disc
geometry (track count, track start frames, lead\-out offset) and matches
only one release in the MusicBrainz database.
.TP
.B acoustid  +0.25
AcoustID per\-track audio fingerprints corroborated the match.
At least one track's Chromaprint fingerprint returned a recording that
agrees with the disc ID or duration\-match release.
.TP
.B mb_duration_match  +0.20
A text search of MusicBrainz (artist + album title) found a release whose
total duration matches the physical disc (last\-resort fallback when the
disc ID returned no results).
.TP
.B isrc_disambiguated  +0.15
Per\-track ISRCs from the Q\-channel broke a tie between multiple
MusicBrainz releases that share the same disc ID, requiring at least two
ISRCs to agree.
.TP
.B cddb_mb_disagreement  \-0.10
The CDDB server's artist or album title string diverges significantly from
the MusicBrainz result, suggesting the CDDB entry may be wrong or the
disc is a re\-press with different metadata.
.SS Recommendation thresholds
.TP
.B STRONG  (score \(>= 0.70)
The pipeline is highly confident.
The recommendation is informational only: the metadata menu is still shown
so the result can be confirmed, with a STRONG recommendation and a one\-line
.IR "Metadata: <score summary>"
hint.
Only
.B \-\-auto
(or
.BR "auto = true" )
skips the menu.
.TP
.B MEDIUM  (score \(>= 0.40)
Two or more independent signals agree.
The metadata menu is shown with a MEDIUM recommendation.
.TP
.B LOW  (score \(>= 0.10)
At least one weak signal matched.
The metadata menu is shown with a LOW recommendation.
.TP
.B NONE  (score < 0.10)
No lookup signals matched.
The metadata menu is shown without a recommendation.
.SS Example scores
.TP
.B 0.90 (STRONG)
Disc ID confirmed in MusicBrainz (+0.50), AcoustID corroborated (+0.25),
ISRCs broke a release tie (+0.15).
.TP
.B 0.45 (MEDIUM)
Duration match only, no disc ID (+0.20), AcoustID corroborated (+0.25).
Typical for a disc not yet catalogued in MusicBrainz by disc ID.
.TP
.B 0.00 (NONE)
No remote lookup returned a usable result (network down, no API
credentials configured, or disc not in any database).
.SS Effect of \-\-auto
Passing
.B \-\-auto
(or setting
.B auto = true
in the configuration) forces
.B auto_apply
unconditionally, regardless of the score.
This is the only way to skip the menu: the recommendation level
.RB ( STRONG ,
MEDIUM, LOW, NONE) never skips it on its own.
.SS AcoustID gate
After the release is selected, a post\-selection AcoustID check fingerprints
tracks 1 and \(lcN/2\(rc and asks whether the disc audio matches the selected
release's
.I album
(matched at the MusicBrainz release\-group level, since AcoustID identifies
recordings rather than pressings).
If the audio does
.I not
corroborate the album \(em a likely wrong disc\-ID match, TOC collision, or
mispress \(em the gate fails:
.B acoustid_gate=failed
is written to provenance, a warning is printed, and
.B \-\-auto
is suppressed for that disc so the result is reviewed rather than
auto\-committed.
The rip is never failed; absence of the key means the gate passed or did not
run.
Inspect failures across a library with
.BR "list \-\-prov" .
.SS MusicBrainz\(->Discogs link check
After the release is selected, the MusicBrainz\(->Discogs url\-relation of the
selected release is followed and the linked Discogs release's barcode is
compared with MusicBrainz's.
This checks the
.I relation,
not the pressing: a MusicBrainz editor supplied both the barcode and the link,
so agreement is not independent confirmation from a second source.
Disagreement is the useful signal \(em positive evidence that the relation
points at the wrong release.
Agreement records
.BR discogs_corroborates=YES ;
disagreement records
.B discogs_corroborates=NO
together with
.B discogs_barcode_conflict=mb:<barcode>|discogs:<barcode>
in provenance.
Absence of the key means the check did not run, which is a different answer
from
.BR NO .
This is informational only \(em it does not affect release selection or
confidence \(em and is skipped entirely when there is no Discogs link, no
.B DISCOGS_TOKEN
configured, or no barcode to compare.
Inspect the result with
.BR "list \-\-prov" .
.\"
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACOUSTID_API_KEY
AcoustID application API key, required for fingerprint lookups during the
interactive metadata menu.
To obtain one, register a free
.I application
(not just a user account) at
.IR acoustid.org .
If unset, AcoustID lookups are silently skipped.
.TP
.B DISCOGS_TOKEN
Discogs personal access token, required for Discogs metadata lookups.
Generate one under Settings\~\(->~Developers at
.IR discogs.com .
If unset, Discogs lookups are silently skipped.
.PP
MusicBrainz lookups require no account or API key.
AccurateRip lookups are anonymous HTTP and require no account or API key.
.\"
.SH CONFIGURATION
cdda2img reads configuration from
.PP
.RS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml
.RE
.PP
When
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset, the default path is
.IR ~/.config/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml .
If the file does not exist and standard input is a terminal,
.B cdda2img rip
will offer to create it automatically from the bundled example file
.RB ( src/cdda2img/conf/cdda2img.toml.example ).
Answer
.B y
at the prompt; the file is created and read before the rip continues.
In non\-interactive contexts (scripts, pipes) a missing file is silently
ignored and all settings use built\-in defaults.
.PP
To create the configuration manually:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkdir \-p ~/.config/cdda2img
cat > ~/.config/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml << 'EOF'
# cdda2img configuration

# CDDB server for disc metadata lookup (host:port).
# cddb_server = "gnudb.gnudb.org:8880"
EOF
.fi
.RE
.SS Configuration keys
.TP
.BI "cddb_server = " \(dqgnudb.gnudb.org:8880\(dq
CDDB server used for automatic disc identification during
.BR "cdda2img rip" .
Format is
.IR host : port .
Default:
.BR gnudb.gnudb.org:8880 .
.TP
.BI "database_backups = " 3
Number of rotating backups to keep for the drive offsets SQLite database.
Set to
.B 0
to disable backups.
Default:
.BR 3 .
.TP
.BI "database_backup_frequency = " \(dq4w\(dq
Minimum interval between automatic drive-offset database backups.
Format:
.IR N \c
.BR d
(days),
.IR N \c
.BR w
(weeks), or
.IR N \c
.BR mo
(months, approximated as 30 days).
Default:
.BR 4w .
.TP
.BI "catalogue_backups = " 3
Number of rotating backups to keep for the disc catalogue database.
Backups are triggered by write access (after each successful rip, import, or create).
Set to
.B 0
to disable backups.
Default:
.BR 3 .
.TP
.BI "catalogue_backup_frequency = " \(dq1d\(dq
Minimum interval between automatic disc catalogue backups.
Accepts the same format as
.BR database_backup_frequency .
Default:
.BR 1d .
.TP
.BI "contact_email = " \(dq\(dq
Email address included in the MusicBrainz API User\-Agent header, as required
by the MusicBrainz terms of service.
Without it, MusicBrainz lookups may be rate\-limited or blocked.
Default: empty.
.TP
.BI "catalogue_path = " \(dqPATH\(dq
Path to the disc catalogue SQLite database.
Default:
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/cdda2img/cdda2img.db
.RI ( ~/.local/share/cdda2img/cdda2img.db ).
.TP
.BI "enable_catalogue = " true
Set to
.B false
to disable automatic catalogue registration after rip, import, or create.
Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.BI "duplicate_catalogue_entry = " \(dqask\(dq
What to do when a disc matching an existing catalogue entry is registered.
.RS
.TP
.B ask
Prompt interactively (default); falls back to
.B skip
when stdin is not a TTY.
.TP
.B skip
Silently abort registration if a matching entry already exists.
.TP
.B replace
Delete the existing entry and insert the new one.
.TP
.B add
Always insert, allowing multiple entries for the same disc.
.RE
Overridable per\-run with
.B \-\-duplicate
on rip, import, and create.
Default:
.BR ask .
.TP
.BI "default_device = " \(dq/dev/sr0\(dq
Default CD drive device used when no
.B \-\-device
argument is supplied.
Default:
.BR /dev/sr0 .
.TP
.BI "silence_threshold = " 55
Silence detection threshold for the
.B create
pipeline, in \-dBFS.
Audio below this level at the head and tail of each track is trimmed when
.B \-\-silence trim
is in effect.
Useful range: 40 (loose) to 70 (strict).
Valid range: 1\(en90.
Default:
.BR 55 .
.TP
.BI "capacity = " 80
Disc capacity in minutes for the
.B create
pipeline batcher.
80 corresponds to a standard 700\~MB CD\-R.
Valid range: 1\(en99.
Default:
.BR 80 .
.TP
.BI "preview = " true
Show a terminal album art preview and play track 1 in the background during
.BR "cdda2img rip" .
Best\-effort and cosmetic; never blocks or fails the rip.
Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.BI "tui = " true
Use the terminal UI for live progress rendering on rip, import, and create.
No\-op when stdin is not a TTY (CI, pipes, etc.).
Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.BI "low_dr_threshold = " 5.0
Album EBU\~R128 loudness range (LU) below which the disc is flagged
.B low_dynamic_range\~=\~YES
in the RBI provenance block and the catalogue.
The default of 5.0\~LU corresponds to a heavily compressed master.
Valid range: 0.5\(en20.0.
Default:
.BR 5.0 .
.TP
.BI "auto = " false
Skip the interactive metadata menu on rip, import, and create.
The pipeline still fetches and applies all metadata; the menu is bypassed
and the best\-guess result is accepted automatically.
Equivalent to always passing
.BR \-\-auto .
Default:
.BR false .
.SS Per-drive offset entries
Per-drive sample offsets are stored as an array of TOML tables under
.BR [[drives]] ,
one table per drive.
Entries are created and updated automatically by
.B cdda2img rip
when a drive offset is confirmed from the AccurateRip catalog.
They can also be set manually:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[[drives]]
name = "PLEXTOR DVDR PX-716A"
read_offset = 30
write_offset = -30
.fi
.RE
.PP
The
.B name
field must match the normalised sysfs drive name printed by
.B cdda2img rip
at rip time.
A per-drive entry is always authoritative and bypasses the AccurateRip catalog lookup.
.\"
.SH HARDWARE SETUP
The
.BR create ,
.BR extract ,
.BR list ,
.BR test ,
and
.B import
subcommands operate entirely on files and require no special hardware access.
.PP
The
.B rip
and
.B burn
subcommands access a physical disc drive.
The optical drive device
.RI ( /dev/sr0
or similar) must be readable (and writable for
.BR burn )
by the user.
On Linux this requires membership in the
.B cdrom
group:
.PP
.RS
.nf
doas usermod \-aG cdrom USERNAME
.fi
.RE
.PP
Log out and back in for the group change to take effect.
Verify access with:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ls \-la /dev/sr0
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Note on vendor\-specific SCSI:
.B cdda2img
does not require root.
Reads go through AccuDisc, which issues standard MMC commands over
.BR SG_IO ;
group membership on the device node is sufficient.
.PP
The distinction matters because the Linux kernel\(cqs SCSI generic driver blocks
.I vendor\-specific
opcodes (0xC0\(en0xFF) from unprivileged users regardless of device group
membership \(em only root, or a process holding
.BR CAP_SYS_RAWIO ,
may issue them.
Some drives expose extra capability behind such opcodes; nothing on
.BR cdda2img \(cqs
path depends on one.
.PP
The
.B mount
subcommand does not access a physical disc drive.
It requires the cdemu daemon to be running and the
.B vhba
kernel module to be loaded.
Start cdemu with:
.PP
.RS
.nf
modprobe vhba
cdemu daemon
.fi
.RE
.\"
.SH SYSTEM DEPENDENCIES
Run
.B cdda2img doctor
to check all of the following on the current machine.
It reports what is missing and what each missing item would have enabled;
it never installs anything.
.SS Required
.TP
.B AccuDisc
The CD\-DA read and write engine
.RI ( https://github.com/HomerSlated/accudisc ),
and the only one.
Required as its
.I Python binding
\(em since 2026\-08\-01
.B cdda2img
calls AccuDisc\(cqs API and never executes its
.B accudisc
binary, so having that binary on
.B $PATH
is not a substitute.
Nothing that touches a physical disc \(em
.BR rip ,
.BR burn ,
.B mount
\(em works without the binding.
Not required for creating, extracting, or verifying RBI images.
.SS Optional
Each of these enables one feature and is skipped cleanly when absent.
.TP
.B ffplay
The rip\(cqs track\-1 preview, which is cosmetic and never fails a rip.
Part of FFmpeg.
Note that audio
.I transcoding
does not need an FFmpeg installation: PyAV carries the FFmpeg libraries
inside its own wheel.
.TP
.B fpcalc
AcoustID audio fingerprinting, part of the Chromaprint library.
Package names:
.B chromaprint
(Void Linux),
.B libchromaprint\-tools
(Debian/Ubuntu).
The AcoustID lookup gates itself on this binary\(cqs presence.
.TP
.B cdemu\-daemon
Required for
.BR "cdda2img mount" .
The cdemu daemon creates virtual CD drives; the
.B vhba
kernel module provides the virtual SCSI host.
Package name:
.B cdemu\-daemon
(most distributions).
.TP
.BR chafa ", " timg ", " kitten
Terminal preview of cover art \(em the first one found is used.
With none of them, artwork is still fetched and stored, just not displayed.
.SS Native libraries
.TP
.B libchromaprint
Loaded at call time by
.BR pyacoustid .
.SS Python packages
In a development checkout, all Python dependencies are installed by
.BR uv :
.PP
.RS
.nf
uv sync
.fi
.RE
.PP
An installed copy gets them from its installer
.RB ( "pipx install ." ,
.BR "pip install ." ).
They are listed, with what each one is for, by
.BR "cdda2img doctor" ;
the same check runs automatically on every invocation and refuses to start
with a list of everything that is missing, rather than an
.B ImportError
naming one package at a time.
.\"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml
User configuration file (global settings and per-drive
.B [[drives]]
entries).
Default location:
.IR ~/.config/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cdda2img/drive_offsets.db
SQLite database caching the AccurateRip drive offset catalog.
Created automatically on first rip.
Default location:
.IR ~/.local/share/cdda2img/drive_offsets.db .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cdda2img/cdda2img.db
Disc catalogue database.
Populated automatically after every rip, import, or create.
Browsable via
.BR "cdda2img catalogue" .
Default location:
.IR ~/.local/share/cdda2img/cdda2img.db .
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
Rip the disc in the default drive:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img rip
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rip from a specific device, skip loudness analysis:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img rip \-\-device /dev/sr0 \-\-loudness none \-\-output mydisc.rbi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create an RBI image from a directory of audio files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img create /music/Technotronic\ \-\ Pump\ Up\ the\ Jam
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create without silence trimming or loudness analysis (1:1 preservation):
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img create /music/album \-\-silence notrim \-\-loudness none
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use global bin\-packing to minimise disc count across a large collection:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img create /music/album \-\-strategy best
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract per\-track FLACs with ReplayGain tags (default):
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img extract album.rbi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract FLACs and also write raw PCM + TOC:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img extract album.rbi \-\-tracks \-\-raw
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract FLACs normalised to \-18\~LUFS:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img extract album.rbi \-\-normalize
.fi
.RE
.PP
Import a cdrdao rip:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img import disc.toc
cdda2img import disc.toc \-\-loudness none \-\-output mydisc.rbi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Import a DDP\~2.0 image directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img import /media/DDP_Technotronic
.fi
.RE
.PP
Import a Nero NRG image:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img import album.nrg
cdda2img import album.nrg \-\-loudness none
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect a PlexTools image without importing it, then import it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img import album.pxi \-\-info
cdda2img import album.pxi
.fi
.RE
.PP
List sections and track listing:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img list album.rbi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify container integrity:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img test album.rbi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Mount an RBI image as a virtual disc via cdemu (into the first free slot):
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img mount album.rbi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Mount into a specific slot and write scratch files to a named directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img mount album.rbi \-\-slot 1 \-\-mnt\-dir /tmp/mnt
.fi
.RE
.\"
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (file not found, unsupported format, checksum mismatch, validation failure).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT
.RB ( Ctrl\-C ).
.\"
